# parse/numbig (id 123): decimal to double for |E10| > 22 (numconv routes here with TK = 11).
# TK 11 = INIT: E10, k = |E10|, e = SIG - 1 + E10, M15 = M 10^(15 - SIG). Overflow (e >= 309, or
# e = 308 and M15 >= 179769313486232) -> TK 11, return. Zero (M = 0, e <= -309, or e = -308 and
# M15 <= 222507385850720, i.e. below 2^-1022) -> TV 0, TK 1, return. Else start the loop with
# h = 2^-512, l = 0, y = 2^512, rem = k, neg = [E10 < 0] in X1..X5 and TK 12.
# TK 12 = LOOP: rem > 0: (h, l) *= D, D = 10^22 (rem > 22) or 10^rem, exact factor, Dekker TwoProduct
# and FastTwoSum; y *= fl(10^-22) or fl(10^-rem); rem -= min(rem, 22). rem = 0: positive: one more
# multiply with D = M, TV = hn 2^512; negative: D = q0 = fl(M y), r = (M - p) - t,
# TV = (q0 + fl(r y)) 2^-512. Return to (X6, X7) with TK 1. Note: weights/parse/numbig.md
input 65
